today we're talking about how lego star  wars has an odd exploit as well as what  lego and epic games are working on and  more  a handy speed running trick has been  found in lego star wars the skywalker  saga which allows players to essentially  fly either vertically or horizontally  across the map as picked up by polygon  the only downside to this trick which  the inventor has named child flight does  unfortunately require the player to beat  up a younglin as posted by twitter user  red orb the latest lego star wars game  doesn't allow child characters to take  friendly fire damage meaning players can  land combo hits on them to fly as far as  they want across quote large pits and  void spaces in a follow-up tweet red orb  explains that the exploit could be used  in a number of different ways with the  game's many jedi characters having  different attack patterns that can be  used to travel in different directions  red orb told polygon quote i play a lot  of devil may cry and other combo games  and saw this game had similar combat red  orb continued was trying stuff on  enemies at first they don't have enough  help tried on the ai player 2 and that  worked better but still too short to be  fun eventually i accidentally hit the  child anakin and he didn't take damage  from there i just used him as a dummy  and found the easiest air loop it'll be  interesting to see how speedrunners end  up using child flight in the skywalker  saga even if it does feel like a very  dark side tactic but hey anakin did it  first in other lego news epic games and  the lego group have announced a  long-term deal to help quote shape the  future of the metaverse and specifically  make it safe and fun for children and  families by metaverse i'm talking about  the general virtual reality digital  world that we're all just eventually  going to live in not necessarily meta as  in facebook details are thin at the  moment but epic and the lego groups said  they will work together to build a quote  immersive creatively inspiring and  engaging digital experience for kids of  all ages to enjoy together the  description goes on to say quote the  family-friendly digital experience will  give kids access to tools that will  empower them to become confident  creators and deliver amazing play  opportunities in a safe and positive  space epic's most popular game fortnite  was not mentioned in the company's press  release so it appears whatever epic and  the lego group are building together no  pun intended is separate from the battle  royale title and in non-lego related  news a remake of max payne and max payne  2 is in the works these remakes are  coming from remedy entertainment the  studio behind the original max payne  games the studio has reached an  agreement with rockstar to remake both  games for pc playstation 5 and series x  and s the remakes will come as a single  release using the north light game  engine which was used for quantum break  and control you shouldn't expect it to  come anytime soon though as the  announcement notes it's only in the  concept development stage max payne was  notable for its neo-noir setting and  bullet time gameplay which became a  mainstay in several other games of the  same era the two games were followed by  max payne 3 of course which was  developed internally at rockstar the  remake project will be financed by  rockstar which the announcement promises  will be treated like a typical  aaa budget production all right now hit  the comment section and let me know how  much i would have to pay you to just  walk across a bunch of legos right now  i'll see you tomorrow  [Music]
 

